          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fractions can be avoided by multiplying both sides of the equation by the least common multiple of the denominators. For example,",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p17-q4-demonstration",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\begin{aligned}&&\\frac12x^2+\\frac13x+\\frac14&=0\\\\(\\times12)&&6x^2+4x+3&=0.\\end{aligned}",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p17-q4-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This gives an equivalent equation whose coefficients are all integers. Solve each of the following equations using this method together with the quadratic formula:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac12x^2+2x-3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2\\pm\\sqrt{10}$",
          "worked": "Multiply by $2$:\n$$x^2+4x-6=0.$$\n$a=1$, $b=4$, $c=-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{4^2-4(1)(-6)}}{2(1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{40}}2\\\\x&=-2\\pm\\sqrt{10}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2-\\frac13x-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{37}}6$",
          "worked": "Multiply by $3$:\n$$3x^2-x-3=0.$$\n$a=3$, $b=-1$, $c=-3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-1)\\pm\\sqrt{(-1)^2-4(3)(-3)}}{2(3)}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{37}}6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac13x^2+\\frac16x-2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{97}}4$",
          "worked": "Multiply by $6$:\n$$2x^2+x-12=0.$$\n$a=2$, $b=1$, $c=-12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{1^2-4(2)(-12)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{97}}4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac12x^2-\\frac14x-\\frac18=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}4$",
          "worked": "Multiply by $8$:\n$$4x^2-2x-1=0.$$\n$a=4$, $b=-2$, $c=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-2)\\pm\\sqrt{(-2)^2-4(4)(-1)}}{2(4)}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{20}}8\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt5}4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^2+\\frac12x-\\frac13=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{57}}{12}$",
          "worked": "Multiply by $6$:\n$$6x^2+3x-2=0.$$\n$a=6$, $b=3$, $c=-2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{3^2-4(6)(-2)}}{2(6)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{57}}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\frac12x^2+\\frac15x-\\frac1{10}=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt6}5$",
          "worked": "Multiply by $10$:\n$$5x^2+2x-1=0.$$\n$a=5$, $b=2$, $c=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{2^2-4(5)(-1)}}{2(5)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt{24}}{10}\\\\x&=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt6}5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
